<Base
  title="About"
  description="About Japanese Knife Archive — the definitive database of Japanese kitchen knives for chefs and cooking enthusiasts worldwide."
>
  <div class="page-header">
    <h1 class="page-header__title">About</h1>
  </div>

  <div class="container container--narrow">
    <div class="article-layout">
      <h2>Japanese Knife Archive</h2>
      <p>
        Japanese Knife Archive is the definitive online database for Japanese kitchen knives.
        We catalog and review knives from Japan's finest bladesmiths — from the legendary
        forges of Sakai and Seki to the innovative workshops of Echizen and Tsubame-Sanjo.
      </p>
      <p>
        Our mission is to help chefs, home cooks, and knife enthusiasts worldwide find the
        perfect Japanese knife for their needs. We provide detailed specifications, steel
        comparisons, and honest reviews based on real-world usage.
      </p>

      <h2>What Makes Us Different</h2>
      <p>
        Unlike generic review sites, we specialize exclusively in Japanese knives. Our steel
        database with radar charts helps you understand exactly what each steel offers. Our
        comparison tool lets you put any two knives side by side. And our magazine articles
        go deep into the craft, history, and science of Japanese bladesmithing.
      </p>

      <h2>Affiliate Disclosure</h2>
      <p>
        Japanese Knife Archive is a participant in affiliate programs including Amazon Associates.
        This means we may earn a small commission when you purchase through our links, at no
        additional cost to you. This helps us maintain and improve this resource.
      </p>
      <p>
        Our reviews and recommendations are independent. Affiliate relationships never influence
        our ratings or which knives we recommend.
      </p>

      <h2>Disclaimer</h2>
      <p>
        The information provided on Japanese Knife Archive is for general informational purposes
        only. While we strive for accuracy, prices, availability, and specifications may change
        without notice. We are not responsible for any purchasing decisions made based on our content.
      </p>
      <p>
        Knife specifications (blade length, weight, hardness, etc.) are sourced from manufacturers
        and may vary slightly between individual units due to the handmade nature of Japanese knives.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Have questions, corrections, or suggestions? We'd love to hear from you.
        <br />Email: info@japaneseknifearchive.com
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
